From 3a6b88413cef18f8b4529ed8740b7cce4d023a21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangjianxin <wangjianxin@canaan-creative.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:01:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Refactor K230 rotation handling into display/input backends

- Move the touch rotation transform from main.c into the evdev
  discovery callback (k230_apply_touch_rotation), eliminating the
  polling loop that waited for async device discovery
- Move the k230_set_drm_rotation() call from main.c into the DRM
  display backend (init_drm) and declare it in lv_linux_drm.h
- drm_k230_v4l2.c: drop its private touch-rotation polling block and
  publish k230_display->drm_rotation as settings.rotation, so both
  executables (lvglsim, lvglsimk230) share the single evdev hook

main.c no longer contains K230-specific code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
